    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d207">

                <pb facs="0169" n="149" sameAs="frus:frus1864p3/pg149"/>

                <head>Mr. F. W. Seward to Mr.
                        Dayton</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 668.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-09-26"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >September</hi> 26, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have received your despatch of the 9th
                    instant, No. 536, which reates to the confederate ships now being built at
                    Bordeaux and Nantes, which <pb facs="0170" n="150" xml:id="pg150"/> is approved.
                    I am pleased to see that you have anticipated and fully executed the
                    instructions contained in a despatch of the 8th of August, No. 629.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>F. W. SEWARD, <hi rendition="#italic">Acting
                    Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">William L. Dayton,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
